    "summary": "**Claim**: Diné Hózhó philosophy operates as a cybernetics of adjustment that restores dynamic balance without monumentalizing or fetishizing injuries.\n\nIn the Diné worldview, when balance is lost ([[Hócho']]), the goal of ceremony and justice is not to display or preserve the scar as an eternal identity or monument, but to re-align internal relations with altered environmental states. This contrasts sharply with Western post-industrial culture, which monument-izes trauma as a spectacle or commodity.\n\nRelated: [[hozho]], [[hocho]], [[cybernetics-of-adjustment]], [[scar-thesis-as-western-diagnostic]], [[sovereign-sanctuary]].",
