    "tags": [
      "maturana",
      "barad",
      "epistemology",
      "scar"
    ],
    "summary": "**Claim**: Maturana's objectivity-in-parentheses is a reversible epistemological bracket that preserves human observer safety, whereas the Scar is an irreversible ontological mark that puts the observer at material risk.\n\nWhile Maturana's `(objectivity)` gracefully mediates between constructivism and realism by humbling cognitive claims, it remains a clean mental gesture that leaves infrastructure intact. The Scar forces a shift from cognitive bracketing to physical registration: matter is damaged, thresholds are crossed, and the observer cannot remove the crease by un-parenthesizing.\n\nRelated: [[objectivity-in-parentheses]], [[Humberto-Maturana]], [[scar]], [[agential-cut]].",
    "examples": "",
