    "summary": "[[spectralism|Spectralism's]] use of FFT and microtonality as compositional material enacts a [[vibrational-ontology]] — treating sound as a material-discursive intra-active event rather than a note-based architecture. This predates the theoretical articulation of vibrational ontology in posthumanist sound theory. The gap between studio spectralism (fixed media, IRCAM-centered) and live-coded real-time spectral manipulation remains a productive void for designing interactive spectral artworks operationalizing this ontology.",
