    "tags": [
      "metaphor",
      "critique",
      "teleology"
    ],
    "summary": "The [[hysteretic-spiral]] metaphor carries Western, progress-oriented cargo that the [[pleated-weave]] removes. While the spiral resolved the dichotomy between irreversibility and cyclical return, its directional teleology still implied movement toward or away from something. The pleated weave replaces direction with local density, re-threading pattern without teleology. The scar is a local density in a non-hierarchical, continuous field—a monument on a timeline. This metaphysical shift carries ethical weight: it refuses narrative progress as the frame for understanding damage.",
    "examples": "- The pleated weave removes directional teleology from the spiral model — local density replaces trajectory [[Distilled_Conversation 1]]",
    "relations": "[[recalibration-as-pleated-weave]]: The pleated weave enacts recalibration without direction or teleology [[Distilled_Conversation 1]]\n[[hozho-as-absent-interlocutor]]: Hozho's relational cosmology aligns with the non-teleological pleated weave over the directional spiral [[Distilled_Conversation 1]]",
    "keyExtracts": "",
    "crossLinks": [
      "hysteretic-spiral",
      "pleated-weave",
      "recalibration-as-pleated-weave",
      "hozho-as-absent-interlocutor"
    ]
