    "summary": "James J. Gibson (1904–1979) — American psychologist who developed the ecological approach to visual perception and the concept of [[affordance-space|affordances]]. Organisms perceive affordances — the invitations and hazards of a world that acts upon them. Affordances arise from the relationship between environment and organism, not from either alone.",
