    "summary": "John D'Agata — American essayist whose philosophy of photography centers on experience over observation. Taking risks makes desire and fear the main principles of existence. \"To understand the world, I have to go to where I am scared of going.\" The single image is a lie because it pretends to condense too many answers in itself.",
