    "summary": "Mary Catherine Bateson (1939–2021), cultural anthropologist, daughter of [[Gregory-Bateson]] and Margaret Mead. Her aphorism \"Each person is his own central metaphor\" crystallizes the [[second-order-cybernetics]] principle that the observer is part of the observation — what we observe is structured by who we are. Her anthropology treats identity as a recursive process aligned with [[constructivism]] and [[autopoiesis]].",
