    "summary": "Michel Serres (1930–2019), French philosopher whose work on noise, the parasite, and communication is synthesized into [[Bruce-Clarke|Clarke]]'s [[neocybernetics]]. His noise concept — the irreducible perturbation that both disrupts and enables communication — resonates with the scar as the residue of the cut that cannot be metabolized. The parasite as noise is both interference and condition of possibility, analogous to the [[blind-spot]] every [[observer]] carries.",
    "examples": "",
