    "summary": "N. Katherine Hayles critiques information's disembodiment in cybernetics — the privileging of pattern over materiality — aligning with the [[erasure-paradigm]] critique the scar concept opposes. Identified as an alternative synthesizer who may explicitly connect [[Niklas-Luhmann|Luhmann]], [[Jacques-Derrida|Derrida]], and cybernetics, Hayles's work on embodied virtuality and the posthuman offers a parallel genealogy for the scar as the material trace first-order cybernetics attempted to erase. The Taylor hypothesis may misattribute the synthesis to a single figure; the scar synthesis may be distributed across multiple thinkers.",
