    "summary": "Artist and researcher whose concept of the experiencer as \"measure of simultaneity\" connects how observers [[intra-action|intra-act]] with and reconfigure space through directed attention. A key question for the [[scar]] thesis: does the technical artwork retain a physical trace of the viewer's presence, or does the \"measure of simultaneity\" exist only as internal perceptual experience? If the encounter is true intra-action, the machine should bear a physical, [[hysteresis|hysteretic]] scar — the artwork as a scarred body recording every encounter.",
    "examples": "",
    "relations": "[[experiencer]] + [[simultaneity]]: Fedorova's \"measure of simultaneity\" — the work unfolds through the viewer's intra-active presence [[Distilled_Scar-Sediment_Feedback_Knot]]\n\n[[intra-action]] + [[scar]]: If the encounter is true intra-action, the artwork must bear a physical, hysteretic scar recording every encounter — the artwork as scarred body [[Distilled_Scar-Sediment_Feedback_Knot]]\n\n[[scar]] + [[model]]: The diffraction verdict identifies shared ground in intra-action but tension on the model's status — \"the scar is not a model, it's the thing itself\"; the cosmotechnic voice later reframes \"correctness\" as ritual adequacy [[Distilled_Scar-Sediment_Feedback_Knot]]\n\n\n- See also: [[scar-as-debt]]",
