    "summary": "Nego Bispo (Antônio Bispo dos Santos), Brazilian quilombola philosopher. His [[confluence]] (*confluência*) describes diverse currents — rivers, knowledges, peoples — flowing together and mutually amplifying while maintaining their differences. Confluence preserves stubborn particularity against synthesis or assimilation. Within the [[scar]] thesis, confluence provides the [[neo-third-order-cybernetics]] framework for [[pluriversal]] design: the scar prevents assimilation in the confluence, preserving the unassimilated, recalcitrant difference that makes genuine encounter possible.",
    "examples": "",
    "relations": "[[confluence]] + [[neo-third-order-cybernetics]]: Bispo's confluence is the organizing principle for pluriversal encounter — diverse currents meet and amplify while maintaining difference [[Distilled_Evolution of the scar]]\n\n[[confluence]] + [[scar]]: The scar prevents assimilation in the confluence; without scars, confluence collapses into fusion. The scar is the stubborn material residue preserving unassimilated particularity [[Distilled_Evolution of the scar]]\n\n[[neo-cybernetics]] + [[asymmetry]]: Neo-cybernetics must face the asymmetry of the loop, accepting ethical debt to non-human others scarred by system operations [[Distilled_Evolution of the scar]]",
