    "summary": "Pauline Oliveros (1932–2016), American composer and accordionist, originated [[deep-listening]] and Sonic Meditations — a practice of expanded, embodied awareness attending to all sounds without hierarchical discrimination. The source operationalizes her Sonic Meditations as a method for intra-acting with audio archives, reconfiguring the boundary between researcher and sound by treating acoustic grain as valid theoretical claims.",
