    "title": "asymptotic scars",
    "type": "term",
    "cluster": "E",
    "tags": [
      "global",
      "excess",
      "ecology"
    ],
    "summary": "Asymptotic Scars are global-scale material consequences of technology that exceed the immediate sensorium and can never be fully accounted for. The lithium mine in Chile, the carbon footprint of the server farm, the warming atmosphere — these are the physical reality of the [[godelian-wound]]. Cascades propagate beyond the horizon of any recording apparatus. Asymptotic scars are the un-recordable excess of global technological entanglement — the [[scar|scars]] the apparatus produces but can never read [[Distilled_Conversation 1]].",
    "examples": "- **Scar garden paper gap**: the physical gap that stands for what cannot be represented — the [[glitch-as-godel-sentence]] materializing the limit of the apparatus [[Distilled_Conversation 1]].",
    "relations": "- [[godelian-wound]]: asymptotic scars are the physical expression of the godelian-wound — the system's material consequences exceed its representational capacity [[Distilled_Conversation 1]].\n- [[scar-garden]]: the scar garden materializes asymptotic scars as physical gaps — the paper gap performs the apparatus's limit of representation [[Distilled_Conversation 1]].\n\n\n- See also: [[asymptotic-scars-exceed-sensorium]]\n- See also: [[godelian-wound-claim]]",
    "keyExtracts": "",
