    "summary": "[[Karen-Barad|Karen Barad]]'s methodological practice of reading texts, phenomena, and concepts through one another — mapping interference patterns where they entangle and diverge rather than seeking reflections or analogies. Diffraction attends to differences that make a difference: where concepts bend, amplify, or cancel each other. In the [[body-without-organs-that-remembers|BwOR]] framework, it is the operative method for synthesizing disparate sources (ice physics, [[kintsugi]] practice, [[spinozist-modalities|Spinozist ontology]], [[decolonial-aesthetics|decolonial critique]]), treating the [[research-membrane]]'s refusals and gaps as [[agential-cut|agential cuts]] that produce determinate exclusions [[Distilled_BwOR_Research_Synthesis]].",
    "examples": "",
    "relations": "- [[agential-cut]]: diffractive reading treats the apparatus's own cuts as constitutive — the synthesis is a \"diffractive cut\" [[Distilled_BwOR_Research_Synthesis]].\n- [[research-membrane]]: the membrane's refusals become sites for further diffractive engagement [[Distilled_BwOR_Research_Synthesis]].\n- [[interferogram]]: the interferogram is the output of diffractive reading — a diagram of conceptual interferences revealing resonances and divergences across frameworks [[Distilled_Diffracting Deleuze, Barad, and Cybernetics]].\n\n\n- See also: [[contradiction-density]]\n- See also: [[diffraction]]\n- See also: [[glitch-fidelity]]\n- See also: [[scar-as-diffraction-pattern]]\n- See also: [[source-entropy]]",
