    "summary": "A **Fissure** is a linear, branching crack that opens within matter when a force exceeds the material's tolerance. Used as an intermediate geometric step between the Deleuzian Fold and the Scar Crevasse, a fissure has directionality from its point of impact but no preset teleology. It represents a permanent material crack through which energy and matter radiate, marking a site of past rupture and ongoing structural strain.\n\nRelated: [[crevasse]], [[hysteretic-fold]], [[material-impedance]], [[scar-as-crevasse-in-matter]].",
