    "summary": "Friction names the necessary collision and resistance without which no material change occurs. Drawing on D&G's concept of [[antiproduction]], the scar thesis asserts friction as the prerequisite of all material agency. Every frictional collision deforms the medium's local curvature, producing the [[scar]] as the persistent record of deformation.",
