    "summary": "Generative systems are process-oriented computational practices where code constitutes the artwork, not auxiliary tooling. The system's state at each moment is a function of its prior state, embedding history in every output. [[software-art]] exemplifies this approach: abstract generative art performs cosmogony, bringing forth an artificial world by declaring its rules of operation.",
