  "infra-sensuous-aesthetics": {
    "id": "infra-sensuous-aesthetics",
    "title": "infra sensuous aesthetics",
    "type": "term",
    "cluster": "C",
    "tags": [
      "aesthetics",
      "non-visual",
      "materiality",
      "epistemology"
    ],
    "summary": "An aesthetics of irreversible intra-action that operates beyond the visual register. Infra-sensuous modalities — tactile, olfactory, radioactive, vibrational, chemical — register material scars without requiring human ocular witness. The scar thesis's visual bias (\"a scar we look at\") occludes agential cuts that escape sensory capture: slow chemical erosion of circuit boards, enzyme cascades in slime mold, radionuclide decay in hardware, electromagnetic field distortion from current leakage. These invisible scars demand reorientation from spectacle to infra-sensuous attunement.",
    "examples": "- **Slime mold metabolism**: enzyme cascades that register as agential cuts without visual trace [[Distilled_Tracing_the_Scar__Material_Agency_from_Feedback_Loops_to_Sed_v1_d4]].\n- **Radioactive decay in hardware**: radionuclide decay as infra-sensuous scar — real but invisible [[Distilled_Tracing_the_Scar__Material_Agency_from_Feedback_Loops_to_Sed_v1_d4]].",
    "relations": "- [[ocularcentrism]]: infra-sensuous aesthetics opposes the visual bias that positions the scar as primarily available for looking [[Distilled_Tracing_the_Scar__Material_Agency_from_Feedback_Loops_to_Sed_v1_d4]].\n- [[non-optical-scar-modalities]]: infra-sensuous aesthetics provides the framework for theorizing scar modalities that escape optical capture [[Distilled_Tracing_the_Scar__Material_Agency_from_Feedback_Loops_to_Sed_v1_d4]].\n- [[forensic-decay]]: slow chemical and radiological erosion as infra-sensuous scar phenomena requiring forensic rather than optical attunement [[Distilled_Tracing_the_Scar__Material_Agency_from_Feedback_Loops_to_Sed_v1_d4]].",
    "keyExtracts": "- \"Non-optical, non-sensory material traces escape the 'look at' paradigm, yet they too are agential cuts\" [[Distilled_Tracing_the_Scar__Material_Agency_from_Feedback_Loops_to_Sed_v1_d4]].\n- \"Scars no less real for being invisible\" [[Distilled_Tracing_the_Scar__Material_Agency_from_Feedback_Loops_to_Sed_v1_d4]].",
    "crossLinks": [
      "ocularcentrism",
      "non-optical-scar-modalities",
      "forensic-decay"
    ]
  },
