    "summary": "An interferogram is a cross-framework concept mapping produced by [[diffractive-reading]] — a diagram of conceptual interferences and reinforcements between disparate theoretical frameworks. In the synthesis of Deleuze, Barad, and cybernetics, the interferogram maps four frameworks across four axes (the temporal cut, relationality, memory and the past, the production of the new), revealing conceptual resonances (e.g., the caesura and the [[agential-cut]]) and divergences. The interferogram makes visible the interference pattern of the diffractive method itself.",
    "examples": "",
    "relations": "- [[diffractive-reading]]: the interferogram is the output of diffractive reading — a diagram of conceptual interferences across frameworks [[Distilled_Diffracting Deleuze, Barad, and Cybernetics]].\n- [[agential-cut]]: the caesura and the agential-cut resonate as conceptual analogues revealed by the interferogram [[Distilled_Diffracting Deleuze, Barad, and Cybernetics]].",
