    "summary": "The **Meta-Scar** refers to the self-inflicted wound on the conceptual apparatus itself, acknowledging that theorizing trauma risks extracting intellectual value from physical wreckage. In the Winnow thesis, the meta-scar is operationalized in Paragraph IV and Zone 4 of the installation, forcing the academic presentation to exhibit its own complicity, energy consumption, and epistemological boundaries rather than offering a clean, domesticated commodity.\n\nRelated: [[academic-extraction]], [[persistent-crease]], [[dead-zone]], [[witness-function]].",
