    "summary": "Neo/third-order cybernetics is an emerging paradigm debated at ASC Brazil 2026, moving beyond closed systems toward [[pluriversal]] design, more-than-human agency, and [[Nego-Bispo]]'s [[confluence]]. Characterized by the shift from closed loops to irreversible historical spirals ([[material-sedimentation|hysteretic-sedimentation]]), acknowledgment of asymmetric material substrates, and embrace of vulnerability, forensic decay, and ethical debt to non-human others. Within the [[scar]]-thesis, the scar becomes the criterion of realness: what prevents assimilation in confluence.",
    "examples": "",
    "relations": "- [[material-sedimentation|hysteretic-sedimentation]]: autopoiesis shifts from closed circle to irreversible historical spiral in neo-third-order cybernetics [[Distilled_Evolution of the scar]].\n- [[confluence]] + [[Nego-Bispo]]: neo-third-order cybernetics emerges from confluence — diverse currents meeting while maintaining differences, with the scar preserving stubborn material residue [[Distilled_Evolution of the scar]].\n- [[asymmetric-accountability]]: neo-cybernetics accepts every recursive loop is supported by an unequal material substrate demanding accountability [[Distilled_Conversation 2]].\n\n- See also: [[cosmotechnics]]\n- See also: [[Heinz-von-Foerster]]\n- See also: [[impaired-viability]]",
