    "summary": "Non-consensual damage names the material harm projected onto substrates and bodies that have no cognitive register of an action yet receive the physical mark. Technical and artistic apparatuses project violent, non-consensual friction onto human, non-human, and mineral substrates — from server farms to marginalized communities — that cannot \"counter-actualize their wounds into poetry.\" They are simply scarred.",
