    "type": "term",
    "cluster": "C",
    "tags": [
      "philosophy",
      "ontology",
      "realism",
      "metaphysics"
    ],
    "summary": "Object-Oriented Ontology (OOO), founded by [[Graham-Harman|Graham Harman]], insists on the [[withdrawal]] of real objects from all relations. Core principles: real objects are never fully accessible to any relation; contact occurs only between [[sensual-object|sensual profiles]]; all entities exist equally as objects ([[flat-ontology]]). Key figures: [[Graham-Harman]], [[Levi-Bryant]], [[Ian-Bogost]], [[Timothy-Morton]].",
    "examples": "",
    "relations": "- [[second-order-cybernetics]]: OOO stands in productive tension with SOC — the cybernetic claim that the observer co-constructs reality pertains only to the sensual realm, never the withdrawn real [[Distilled_Lets_make_analysis_of_idea_of_cybernetic_observer_in_OOO_v0_d1]].\n- [[cybernetic-observer]]: OOO's cybernetic observer is a scarred hybrid — SOC's radical constructivism embraced for the sensual realm, while the real object remains a constitutive blind-spot [[Distilled_Lets_make_analysis_of_idea_of_cybernetic_observer_in_OOO_v0_d1]].\n- [[onticology]]: Bryant's onticology is a variant of OOO with cybernetic-inflected machine ontology [[Distilled_Lets_make_analysis_of_idea_of_cybernetic_observer_in_OOO_v0_d1]].\n- [[Andrew-Pickering]]: Pickering's performative ontology resists OOO's withdrawal — observer and observed are entangled and co-constituted [[Distilled_Lets_make_analysis_of_idea_of_cybernetic_observer_in_OOO_v0_d1]].\n- [[Donna-Haraway]]: Haraway's situated knowledges, diffracted through Barad and OOO, challenge the minimal observer's universalist assumptions [[Distilled_Lets_make_analysis_of_idea_of_cybernetic_observer_in_OOO_v0_d1]].\n\n- See also: [[bryants-onticology-bridges-soc-ooo]]\n- See also: [[dance-of-agency]]\n- See also: [[eigenform-ontological-ambiguity]]\n- See also: [[harman-silence-on-cybernetics]]\n- See also: [[Heinz-von-Foerster]]\n- See also: [[machine-oriented-ontology]]\n- See also: [[mangle-of-practice]]\n- See also: [[performative-ontology]]\n- See also: [[quadruple-object]]\n- See also: [[Rahma-Khazam]]\n- See also: [[vicarious-causation]]",
    "keyExtracts": "- \"Real objects are never fully accessible to any relation\" [[Distilled_Lets_make_analysis_of_idea_of_cybernetic_observer_in_OOO_v0_d1]].",
