    "summary": "[[Maturana-Varela|Maturana]]'s term for the classical realist stance: the observer assumes an independent objective reality exists prior to and separate from observation, serving as truth's ultimate validator. Maturana associates this path with [[transcendental-ontology]]. Both [[second-order-cybernetics|Second-Order Cybernetics]] and [[Karen-Barad|Barad]]'s [[agential-realism]] reject this as the [[god-trick]].",
    "examples": "",
