    "relations": "- [[post-digital-aesthetics]] + [[glitch-theory]]: Glitch is the post-digital condition itself — the constitutive ground of digital materiality [[Distilled_Lets_make_a_research_for_the_audio_part_of_the_artwork__The__v0_d2]].\n- [[post-digital-aesthetics]] + [[glitch-music]]: Post-digital aesthetics provides the broader frame within which glitch music operates — error as condition, not genre [[Distilled_Lets_make_a_research_for_the_audio_part_of_the_artwork__The__v0_d2]].\n- [[post-digital-aesthetics]] + [[digital-kintsugi]]: Both frameworks address the material substrate of digital media — kintsugi as repair practice, post-digital as the recognition that breakage is the ground [[Distilled_Lets_make_a_research_for_the_audio_part_of_the_artwork__The__v0_d2]].\n\n\n- See also: [[Oval]]",
