    "summary": "The **Sovereign Sanctuary** (Zone 5 of the ASC Brazil 2026 installation score) is an un-wired, un-instrumented plot of native soil and living plants situated at the physical center of the gallery. Designed to prevent epistemic extraction and colonial appropriation of Diné [[Hózhó]] cosmology, the sanctuary contains no electricity, sensors, cameras, or data collection. It functions as a physical boundary where cybernetic apparatuses must halt, confess their internal blindness, and bow, establishing an un-penetrable sanctuary of silence and non-extractive relation.\n\nRelated: [[hozho]], [[hozho-refuses-monumentalizing-injury]], [[scar-thesis-as-western-diagnostic]], [[decolonial-aesthetics]].",
