    "summary": "The philosophical position that sound is fundamentally vibrational matter — not a secondary quality or subjective perception but a real, material force. It treats sound as vibration before representation, as material intra-action before cultural meaning. [[spectralism|Spectralism's]] historical use of FFT as compositional material prefigures a vibrational ontology — treating sound as a phenomenological intra-active event rather than note-based architecture. The vibrational ontology aligns with [[Karen-Barad]]'s agential realism: sound as vibration is the material-discursive field from which determinate sonic phenomena are resolved through [[agential-cut|agential cuts]].",
    "examples": "",
    "relations": "- [[vibrational-ontology]] + [[spectralism]]: Spectralism's FFT-based composition prefigures vibrational ontology — sound as intra-active event [[Distilled_Lets_make_a_research_for_the_audio_part_of_the_artwork__The__v0_d2]].\n- [[vibrational-ontology]] + [[sonic-flux]]: Sonic flux provides the ontological ground for treating sound as matter-in-vibration [[Distilled_Lets_make_a_research_for_the_audio_part_of_the_artwork__The__v0_d2]].\n- [[vibrational-ontology]] + [[vibrant-matter]]: Vibrant matter extends vibrational ontology into political ecology — material agency as active, not passive [[Distilled_Lets_make_a_research_for_the_audio_part_of_the_artwork__The__v0_d2]].\n- [[vibrational-ontology]] + [[agential-realism]]: Sound as vibration is the material-discursive field resolved into determinate sonic phenomena through agential cuts [[Distilled_Lets_make_a_research_for_the_audio_part_of_the_artwork__The__v0_d2]].\n- [[Christoph-Cox]]: Cox's sonic flux provides the ontological ground for vibrational ontology — sound as real material force preceding human perception [[Distilled_Lets_make_a_research_for_the_audio_part_of_the_artwork__The__v0_d2]].\n- [[Eliane-Radigue]]: Radigue's ARP 2500 drone practice exemplifies vibrational ontology made manifest through analog synthesis [[Distilled_Lets_make_a_research_for_the_audio_part_of_the_artwork__The__v0_d2]].\n\n\n- See also: [[acoustic-ecology]]\n- See also: [[deep-listening]]\n- See also: [[fft-spectral-processing]]\n- See also: [[humanesis]]\n- See also: [[Jane-Bennett]]\n- See also: [[microsound]]\n- See also: [[sound-as-material-substance-perceptual-coherence]]\n- See also: [[spectralism-enacts-vibrational-ontology]]",
