    "summary": "[[Graham-Harman]]'s concept for how objects interact without direct contact — causation is indirect, mediated through [[sensual-object|sensual profiles]], never a direct transaction between real objects. Real objects are separated by a permanent gap ([[withdrawal]]). This contrasts with [[Andrew-Pickering]]'s [[mangle-of-practice]], where entities mutually transform one another in direct [[entanglement]]. The tension between vicarious causation and the mangle is a central axis of the OOO-cybernetics difraction.",
