    "summary": "Musical practices using tuning systems outside the standard 12-tone equal temperament — encompassing microtonal, just intonation, and non-Western tuning systems. Xenharmonics risks being treated as an \"exoticised add-on\" within Western experimental music discourse: non-Western music theories reduced to their tuning systems rather than engaged as foundational epistemologies. It forms part of a cross-genre aesthetic of sound-as-material-substance alongside [[spectralism]] and [[glitch-music|glitch]].",
