    "relations": "- [[xenharmonics]] + [[spectralism]]: Both treat sound as material substance — xenharmonics through tuning, spectralism through timbral analysis [[Distilled_Lets_make_a_research_for_the_audio_part_of_the_artwork__The__v0_d2]].\n- [[xenharmonics]] + [[euclidean-rhythms]]: Part of the broader experimental music landscape exploring non-standard temporal and tonal structures [[Distilled_Lets_make_a_research_for_the_audio_part_of_the_artwork__The__v0_d2]].\n- [[xenharmonics]] + [[microsound]]: Microsound and xenharmonics share concern with sound at the limits of perceptual resolution — time and tuning [[Distilled_Lets_make_a_research_for_the_audio_part_of_the_artwork__The__v0_d2]].",
